NAME
       getenv, setenv, unsetenv, putenv - the environment

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdlib.h>

       char *getenv(const char *name);
       int   setenv(const char *name, const char *value, int overwrite);
       int   unsetenv(const char *name);
       int   putenv(char *string);

DESCRIPTION
       Reads and changes the environment of the calling process. The
       environment is inherited across fork and, unlike some minimal
       systems, across execve as well, so HOME and PATH survive into a
       program a shell starts.

       putenv keeps the caller's string rather than copying it, so that
       string must stay valid.

RETURN VALUE
       getenv returns the value or NULL. The others return 0, or -1
       with errno set.

SEE ALSO
       execve(2), env(1), csh(1)
